.nh
.TH "PB-ENV-ROTATE-CANCEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-rotate-cancel - Cancel an uncommitted personal ENV key rotation


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env rotate cancel [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Cancel an uncommitted personal ENV key rotation

.PP
Cancel an uncommitted personal key rotation using the exact confirmation. A completed rotation cannot be undone by this command.

.PP
ENV values are encrypted before they leave the client. Commands select personal, team, or host scope explicitly; list output shows metadata rather than secret values. Unlock the local vault when a key operation requires it.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	exact confirmation phrase: CANCEL ENV ROTATE <account_id>

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for cancel

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env-rotate(1)\fP
